  "cli_result_text": "Submitted the file set required to trace both sides of the contract:\n\n**FastAPI request validation chain:**\n- `fastapi/routing.py` \u2014 `content_type_value = request.headers.get(\"content-type\")` negotiation, body-await (`request.json()`/`request.body()`), and dispatch into dependency solving.\n- `fastapi/dependencies/utils.py` \u2014 `request_body_to_args`, `solve_dependencies`, `get_body_field`, embed logic for single vs. multi-field bodies.\n- `fastapi/_compat.py` \u2014 Pydantic v1/v2 compat shim (`ModelField.validate`/`.serialize`, `create_body_model`), where None/missing/default handling actually resolves.\n- `fastapi/encoders.py` \u2014 `jsonable_encoder`, the asymmetric counterpart used server-side for non-JSON-native types.\n- `fastapi/params.py`, `fastapi/exceptions.py` \u2014 `Body(embed=...)` field definitions and `RequestValidationError`/422 shape.\n\n**httpx request encoding chain:**\n- `httpx/_content.py` \u2014 `encode_json` (bare `json.dumps`, no custom encoder), `encode_request` content/data/files/json precedence.\n- `httpx/_models.py` \u2014 `Request.__init__`/`_prepare`, Content-Type/Content-Length header derivation.\n- `httpx/_client.py` \u2014 `build_request`, where `json=` is accepted from the caller.\n- `httpx/_utils.py` \u2014 `primitive_value_to_str` (None \u2192 `\"\"` for form/query encoding, relevant contrast to JSON's `null`).\n- `httpx/_types.py`, `httpx/_multipart.py` \u2014 type contracts and multipart encoding path.\n\nThis gives the full FastAPI validation chain and full httpx encoding chain plus the exact functions where the drift (embed/nested-model shape, None-vs-missing, Union discrimination, non-JSON-native type serialization) originates on each side.",
